From 6e3d349db489046e38b15dc6ce2aef87558cf951 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 18:11:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix high-priority UX audit findings (dashboard greeting,
 print CSS, remember-me, visit/collection linkage, selected-state contrast,
 login page)

- Dashboard greeting now binds to the logged-in operator instead of the
  first urgent-worklist patient's name (confirmed live bug).
- Hardcoded '1 STAT pending' text now derives from the live worklist.
- Disambiguated the two 'samples' figures on the dashboard welcome band.
- Added a global @media print rule in styles.css to hide the fixed
  sidebar/topbar chrome on every dashboard page (report-preview's
  component-scoped print styles couldn't reach them under
  ViewEncapsulation), plus print-color-adjust on flag/status colors.
- 'Remember me' now persists the actual session, not just the username,
  so a page refresh no longer bounces a remembered operator to login.
- Visit type and Sample collection on Patient Registration no longer
  silently contradict each other; Home visit auto-derives Home
  collection, with manual override still allowed.
- Selected segmented-control state (Appointment/Non-fasting etc.) now
  differs from unselected by two visual channels (fill + heavier
  border) instead of a faint tint alone, fixing weak light-mode
  contrast.
- Fixed production build config: angular.json had no fileReplacements,
  so environment.production stayed false in production builds,
  meaning the demo-credential login hint would ship to real users.
- Replaced the dead 'Forgot password?' link with a button that
  honestly surfaces that self-service reset isn't available yet,
  instead of going nowhere.
- Strengthened the login field focus indicator (was outline:none +
  a 1px color-only border shift) to a two-channel border + visible
  focus ring.
